--TEST--
each of the six magic method names `rule:classes/no-magic-methods` closes is refused where it is written, so no class can declare one for the runtime to decline to call — `rule:classes/stringable`, `rule:classes/no-destructors`, `rule:classes/unset-is-refused-on-a-property`, `rule:classes/no-debug-hook` and `rule:classes/no-magic-methods`, `rule:core-api/casing-checks-the-leading-character`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:classes/no-magic-methods` is the index of every magic method's disposition, and for the six
// names it closes itself the disposition is one and the same: the name cannot
// be written at all. `rule:core-api/casing-checks-the-leading-character`'s method-casing rule refuses a leading
// underscore before any resolution runs, so "the runtime never invokes it" is
// stronger than the ADR's own wording — there is no declaration to invoke.
class Legacy {
    public string $name = "boxy";

    // § 1: `Stringable::toString` is the replacement, and the rename the
    // diagnostic suggests is the one `nvs convert` makes at M11.
    public function __toString(): string {
        return $this->name;
    }

    // § 2: Novis has no destructors, which is why "no `__destruct` runs when a
    // refcount reaches zero" needs no running program to verify.
    public function __destruct(): void {
    }

    // § 3: neither name has anything left to intercept, so neither needs a
    // replacement; what the two constructs now mean is pinned by
    // `isset-answers-a-null-test-over-every-storage-shape.nvst` and by
    // `unset-is-refused-on-a-declared-property.nvst`.
    public function __isset(string $n): bool {
        return true;
    }

    public function __unset(string $n): void {
    }

    // § 4: a dump shows the declared properties and their live values, never
    // what a class chose to substitute for them.
    public function __debugInfo(): array<mixed> {
        return [];
    }

    // § 5: reconstructing an object from data is `rule:classes/two-copy-depths`'s closed round trip.
    public static function __set_state(array<mixed> $s): Legacy {
        return new Legacy();
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";

// The marker sits below the last refused line on purpose: the anchors in
// `--EXPECTF-ERROR--` are absolute, so a line added above one moves it.
// covers: lang:classes/what-a-class-cannot-declare
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0111]: method names must be camelCase, e.g. `toString`
   --> case.nvs:12:21
%A
error[E0111]: method names must be camelCase, e.g. `destruct`
   --> case.nvs:18:21
%A
error[E0111]: method names must be camelCase, e.g. `isset`
   --> case.nvs:25:21
%A
error[E0111]: method names must be camelCase, e.g. `unset`
   --> case.nvs:29:21
%A
error[E0111]: method names must be camelCase, e.g. `debugInfo`
   --> case.nvs:34:21
%A
error[E0111]: method names must be camelCase, e.g. `setState`
   --> case.nvs:39:28
%A
